-- **The `retry` wait stays a counting `for`, and clang stays silent: the shape probe
-- of the lane-73 `for`-loop repair.**
--
-- The bounded wait lowers to a loop whose condition names a value no statement of
-- the body writes (here the parameter `bereit`): the exit runs through the named
-- `on_exceeded` arm, and the body only steps the watchdog counter. Under
-- `clang -Wall -Wextra -Werror` the lane-142 shape `for (; !(bereit); )` fires
-- `-Wfor-loop-analysis` (*variable 'bereit' used in loop condition not modified
-- in loop body*), while gcc stays silent -- measured 2026-09-12 on
-- `beispiele/66-transport-rueckgabe.gab` (clang 18.1.3 fires, gcc 13.3.0 silent,
-- at `-O0` and `-O2` alike). That warning fires exactly when NO variable of the
-- condition is modified in the body or the increment -- so the watchdog counter
-- stands in the header AND the condition:
-- `for (; !(bereit) && _r1 < 1024u; _r1 += 1)`, and the bound arm stands after
-- the loop: `if (_r1 >= 1024u && !(bereit)) { haengt(); }`. A `while` would be
-- silent too, but `while` was lowered away on purpose (CForm census) and stays
-- lowered away: this repair widens no admitted form.
--
-- This file pins the SHAPE, not just the acceptance: the emitted C must carry the
-- counting `for` above and the trailing bound arm, and no `while`. The acceptance
-- itself -- every emitting unit compiling under both compilers -- is held by
-- stage 9 of `instrumente/pruefe-emission.sh`, which runs `cc` and `clang` side
-- by side.
--
-- Counterpart: `messung/proben/emission-142/probe-142-retry-for.gab` documents the
-- lane-142 shape this repair extends (counter into the condition, arm after the
-- loop).

module probe::wieder73 {

extern fn haengt() -> never effects { diverges } costs <= 1 ops;

impl fn warten(bereit : bool) -> bool
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 2048 ops
{
    retry schleife until bereit
        bounded 1024 ops
        on_exceeded haengt
        effects { pure }
    { }
    return bereit;
}

}
